{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiggingError"},{"type":"text","text":" is an error that knows how to dig deeper into its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"underlying context to attempt to pull out a more granular reason for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failure."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiggingError","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice (currently) such digging only occurs when there is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that fails to decode and that presents an opportunity to do one of three things:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Present the error that neither of two things decoded successfully."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Present the error that thing 1 failed to decode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Present the error that thing 2 failed to decode.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The reason it ever makes sense to only present an error from one of the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branches is that sometimes we can heuristically determine that it was exceedingly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unlikely the user intended to represent the thing from the other branch. This error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol is all about determining whether that is the case or not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"T